(2927503, 404504, 48389, '<td valign="top">wow some of your commenters have looked really closely! I sure didn''t see you reflected in the pearls! I have to agree that getting rid of the marks on the egg (by moving its position?) may have helped your score a bit here. The background looks a little pixalised to me mainly on the top right handside and I am not a huge fan of the central position of the objects. I think you have met what I believed the challenge to mean and you have gathered exactly 2 objects so for me that gave you a few extra marks! Yanko''s B&amp;W idea sounds interesting, I wonder whether this would have more impact if you tried that?</td>', 'wow some of your commenters have looked really closely! I sure didn''t see you reflected in the pearls! I have to agree that getting rid of the marks on the egg (by moving its position?) may have helped your score a bit here. The background looks a little pixalised to me mainly on the top right handside and I am not a huge fan of the central position of the objects. I think you have met what I believed the challenge to mean and you have gathered exactly 2 objects so for me that gave you a few extra marks! Yanko''s B&W idea sounds interesting, I wonder whether this would have more impact if you tried that?', '2006-10-14 01:03:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2927609, 404504, 31399, '<td valign="top">sorry not to have commented on this already...no phone line yet for cut from plumber...grrrr<br/> <br/>thinking on DPC past tactics I''ve read, can you spray "pam" on an egg to make it shiny? and I think the shadow on right hand pearls detracts.  But I LIKE this shot.  I''m rather skidish to comment critique wise because I LOVE your work and feel you know technical need for a shot MUCH better than I.  so my comments are more what would make ME purchase the picture.  Egg being more symmetrical vertical and perhaps in right or left 2/3 of frame I think.  You rock and very creative idea...</td>', 'sorry not to have commented on this already...no phone line yet for cut from plumber...grrrr thinking on DPC past tactics I''ve read, can you spray "pam" on an egg to make it shiny? and I think the shadow on right hand pearls detracts.  But I LIKE this shot.  I''m rather skidish to comment critique wise because I LOVE your work and feel you know technical need for a shot MUCH better than I.  so my comments are more what would make ME purchase the picture.  Egg being more symmetrical vertical and perhaps in right or left 2/3 of frame I think.  You rock and very creative idea...', '2006-10-14 02:01:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2927658, 404504, 45475, '<td valign="top">I like the concept. Without the title, I wouldn''t have got it. However, connection or not, it''s still a technically sound image. My thoughts on this echo the other commenters with respect to spots and egg position, but I also wondered if a different perspective may have lifted this? Maybe level with the egg rather than a downward point of view? Just a thought :)</td>', 'I like the concept. Without the title, I wouldn''t have got it. However, connection or not, it''s still a technically sound image. My thoughts on this echo the other commenters with respect to spots and egg position, but I also wondered if a different perspective may have lifted this? Maybe level with the egg rather than a downward point of view? Just a thought :)', '2006-10-14 02:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2927966, 404660, 51538, '<td valign="top">I liked everything about this photo and gave it a 7 - expect for the blue/purple shadow around the bowl.  I would have dodged it out or something.  I would also have left the spoon out too.  But overall, nice placing.</td>', 'I liked everything about this photo and gave it a 7 - expect for the blue/purple shadow around the bowl.  I would have dodged it out or something.  I would also have left the spoon out too.  But overall, nice placing.', '2006-10-14 09:29:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2928084, 404709, 11854, '<td valign="top">I really like this one Deb! But, then it''s the type of image I would normally produce. Very quirky! Of course, I wouldn''t have gotten anywhere near a 5 if I had done this. Adding to my favs!</td>', 'I really like this one Deb! But, then it''s the type of image I would normally produce. Very quirky! Of course, I wouldn''t have gotten anywhere near a 5 if I had done this. Adding to my favs!', '2006-10-14 10:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2928112, 401905, 11854, '<td valign="top">Nice shot! Though I like spiders, I still wouldn''t touch one! Focus is spot on (as you noted) and the spider is cute. Your score is quite decent given all the bug &amp; blank haters on the site. I didn''t vote in this one but would have given it at least an 8.</td>', 'Nice shot! Though I like spiders, I still wouldn''t touch one! Focus is spot on (as you noted) and the spider is cute. Your score is quite decent given all the bug & blank haters on the site. I didn''t vote in this one but would have given it at least an 8.', '2006-10-14 11:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2929539, 404646, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>I find the lighting of the duck to be a bit bright.  The duck almost blends with the background at the tail.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field are quite good and fit the image well.<br/> <br/>Interesting take on the challenge.  Both are poultry.  But one is kitchen and one is bath.  Nice subtle message.  <br/> <br/>I like this picture, but I find the idea of a slightly different angle that would further emphasize the height of the wisk even more, an atttractive idea.<br/> <br/>Nice bit of humor.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: I find the lighting of the duck to be a bit bright.  The duck almost blends with the background at the tail. Focus and depth of field are quite good and fit the image well. Interesting take on the challenge.  Both are poultry.  But one is kitchen and one is bath.  Nice subtle message.   I like this picture, but I find the idea of a slightly different angle that would further emphasize the height of the wisk even more, an atttractive idea. Nice bit of humor.', '2006-10-15 02:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2929556, 404554, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Focus is good.  Color, saturation and hue are done well.<br/> <br/>The lighting is a little harsh and the reflected highlights on the paper are a little distracting.  <br/> <br/>I''m not sure about the significance of the drops of liquid on the paper.  Spilt whiskey?  Tears?  Drool?<br/> <br/>I would have liked this better if the label were easier to read.  You really have to work a bit to make out the word "Scotch".  Rotating the bottle a bit would have helped.  As would have a shallower angle.<br/> <br/>I noted the title was defiance.  Perhaps a poured glass of scotch would have been in order.  Or even a partially consumed, or almost empty glass would also help communicate the notion.<br/> <br/>Interesting start on a composition with some potential.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Focus is good.  Color, saturation and hue are done well. The lighting is a little harsh and the reflected highlights on the paper are a little distracting.   I''m not sure about the significance of the drops of liquid on the paper.  Spilt whiskey?  Tears?  Drool? I would have liked this better if the label were easier to read.  You really have to work a bit to make out the word "Scotch".  Rotating the bottle a bit would have helped.  As would have a shallower angle. I noted the title was defiance.  Perhaps a poured glass of scotch would have been in order.  Or even a partially consumed, or almost empty glass would also help communicate the notion. Interesting start on a composition with some potential.', '2006-10-15 02:44:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2929633, 403786, 43115, '<td valign="top"><b><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/>First Impression - the most important one:</b> Aww!  How cute!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> This photo follows the rule of thirds nicely.  The viewer is immediatley drawn to the baby, then the round frame of the drum leads the viewer''s eye nicely around the perimiter of the photo, and right back into the main subject.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> Aww, cute and cuddly.  The expression is great!  This photo really speaks from the heart.  The viewer can easily tell that the photograph was taken with love.  The message is obvious in this one.  Unfortunatly for your score, the photo lacks the "wow appeal" that makes winners here.  Notice my first impression was "aww," not "wow."<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b>  Quite well done.  I imagine this was a bit of a complex setup, but you got the lighting just right.  Not too much, though there could be a little less.  Don''t get me wrong, I like it just the way it is... but I think it also could have been nice with some more shadow and mood.<br/> <br/><b>Relation to the Challenge:</b> Yep, two, unrelated objects.  Check.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> Meh.  I don''t know that this subject is one that <i>can</i> score really highly here, at least if it''s not the most incredible, moody, wonderfuly lit baby portrait possible.  But I don''t think you should care... this is a photo you can cherish, even if the rest of us don''t think that its the best thing since Ansel Adams.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> I think this is a photo you can be proud of, and something I would frame and put on my desk.  It is quite nice, and you got a nice score.  Keep shooting!<br/> <br/><b>Critique the Critique:</b> A lot of effort goes into writing these critiques and I would appreciate feedback on how I''m doing. Do my comments make sense? Am I on track or way off base? Do my comments make you want to pick up a meat cleaver? Please let me know via a PM if you found these comments helpful, or not so much so.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  First Impression - the most important one: Aww!  How cute! Composition: This photo follows the rule of thirds nicely.  The viewer is immediatley drawn to the baby, then the round frame of the drum leads the viewer''s eye nicely around the perimiter of the photo, and right back into the main subject. Subject: Aww, cute and cuddly.  The expression is great!  This photo really speaks from the heart.  The viewer can easily tell that the photograph was taken with love.  The message is obvious in this one.  Unfortunatly for your score, the photo lacks the "wow appeal" that makes winners here.  Notice my first impression was "aww," not "wow." Technical (Colour and light):  Quite well done.  I imagine this was a bit of a complex setup, but you got the lighting just right.  Not too much, though there could be a little less.  Don''t get me wrong, I like it just the way it is... but I think it also could have been nice with some more shadow and mood. Relation to the Challenge: Yep, two, unrelated objects.  Check. To grow its vote?: Meh.  I don''t know that this subject is one that can score really highly here, at least if it''s not the most incredible, moody, wonderfuly lit baby portrait possible.  But I don''t think you should care... this is a photo you can cherish, even if the rest of us don''t think that its the best thing since Ansel Adams. Summary: I think this is a photo you can be proud of, and something I would frame and put on my desk.  It is quite nice, and you got a nice score.  Keep shooting! Critique the Critique: A lot of effort goes into writing these critiques and I would appreciate feedback on how I''m doing. Do my comments make sense? Am I on track or way off base? Do my comments make you want to pick up a meat cleaver? Please let me know via a PM if you found these comments helpful, or not so much so.', '2006-10-15 04:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
